{
  "issue_date": "2025-10-03",
  "report_week": 40,
  "year": 2025,
  "quote_of_the_week": {
    "type": "Quote of the Week",
    "quote": "When mooncakes are shared, business takes a break.",
    "author": "Chinese proverb"
  },
  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "Our Chinese friends are currently away for Golden Week (October 1st-8th), celebrating the \nMid-Autumn Festival with traditional mooncakes and lanterns. With multiple holidays across the Far \nEast - including South Korea (October 3rd-9th) - the s+p market has a quieter feel (and \nsignificantly fewer emails!). That said, a notable wave of transactions emerged as numerous buyers \nrushed to conclude business ahead of the break at firm levels. \n \nUncertainty prevails in the chartering market this week, as Charterers are holding back most cargoes in \nthe hopes of securing lower rates. The exception to this is the US Gulf, where there is more activity, \nalong with cautious optimism for East Coast South America cargoes within the coming weeks.",
    "tankers": "Europeans are splashing the cash ($472 million) in four VLCC resales (Tier 3, scrubber \nfitted) from Hengli Dalian Shipyard, with deliveries scheduled for 2026.",
    "demolition": "The markets in the sub-continent are more or less stable. For an overview of demolition \nmarket rates this week, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
